Credits
-------

Rainmeter - https://rainmeter.net - https://github.com/rainmeter/rainmeter
  By the Rainmeter team, licensed under the GNU GPL v2.
  RainTux brings Rainmeter's skins to Linux. It reads Rainmeter's skin format (.ini skins,
  .rmskin packages, layouts) and follows Rainmeter's behaviour; Rainmeter's source code was the
  reference for how options, bangs, measures, meters and the Lua scripting API work. RainTux is a
  separate program written in Python for Linux. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
  Rainmeter team; "Rainmeter" is their name and is used here only to describe compatibility.

